From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report a re-protected image page as copied.

Windows maps a writable image section copy-on-write and reports a page
as PAGE_WRITECOPY until it is written, then as PAGE_READWRITE. Wine maps
such pages writable from the start, never sees the write, and reported
PAGE_WRITECOPY as the old protection whatever had happened to the page.
Chromium protects a page of its own data read-only after writing it and
ends the process unless VirtualProtect reports exactly PAGE_READWRITE:
Battle.net.exe stopped a second after its window appeared, on the
console and under the same Wine on the PC.

A program that re-protects an image page has written it, so report the
copied form, as Proton does with WINE_SIMULATE_WRITECOPY. Nothing else
changes: the page's mapping and later queries are as before.

 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index aba21c6f4b..8cf36c581d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5933,7 +5933,15 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtProtectVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SIZE_T
         /* Make sure all the pages are committed */
         if (get_committed_size( view, base, size, &vprot, VPROT_COMMITTED ) >= size && (vprot & VPROT_COMMITTED))
         {
-            old = get_win32_prot( vprot, view->protect );
+            /* Windows reports a writable image page as PAGE_READWRITE once
+             * it has been written, and the program that re-protects one has
+             * written it: its data lives there. Wine maps such pages writable
+             * from the start and never sees the write, so report the copied
+             * form; Chromium checks for exactly PAGE_READWRITE here. */
+            if ((view->protect & SEC_IMAGE) && (vprot & VPROT_WRITECOPY))
+                old = get_win32_prot( (vprot & ~VPROT_WRITECOPY) | VPROT_WRITE, view->protect );
+            else
+                old = get_win32_prot( vprot, view->protect );
             status = set_protection( view, base, size, new_prot );
         }
         else status = STATUS_NOT_COMMITTED;
